## SQL Analysis
Overview

This folder contains the SQL queries used to investigate employee attrition patterns in the IBM HR Analytics dataset.

## Objectives

The SQL analysis explores workforce attrition to identify employee groups and workplace factors associated with 
employees leaving the organisation.

## Key questions include:

Which departments have higher attrition rates?
How does attrition vary with employee tenure?
What patterns exist between overtime and attrition?
Which employee characteristics may warrant further investigation?

## Tools
SQL
MySQL Workbench
Analytical Approach

SQL was used to query, filter, aggregate, and analyse employee records to identify attrition patterns and generate 
insights for further statistical analysis and visualisation.

## Files

The SQL scripts in this folder contain the queries developed for the project.

## Key Takeaway

SQL provides a structured way to examine employee data, quantify attrition patterns, and support 
evidence-based HR decision-making.
